# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to answer to no one (B; cycle s3)

== the first money earned with no one over you
tier: life event
aim: to answer to no one
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 16-60
per_year: 0 0 .5 .4 .3 0
tone: joy
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent, neighbour, a customer
earth: a first Saturday working a stall of your own, with no boss and no rota
tribal: a first trip alone to the trading ground, with skins of your own to barter
magic: a first day at a free stall on the crossroads, with no guild master watching
scene: It is seven on a Saturday and {N} is setting out a folding table at the market: a cash tin, a hand-painted sign, and nobody to answer to.
scene W: {N} has written out a price list and means to keep every price on it, whatever the stall opposite does.
scene U: {N} counted the people passing this pitch for three Saturdays, and chose it for the morning sun.
scene B: Every coin in that tin will be {Ns} own. Nobody takes a cut, and nobody signs off the hours.
scene R: {N} walked out of the café on Thursday in the middle of a shift, and this table is the reason.
scene G: The stall sells jam and chutney from {grandparent}'s old recipes, and the jars look like home.
- W | keep to the posted prices and give honest change all day | v: conformity, universalism (fairness) | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U | note every sale in a little book and work out what really sells | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: lesson the numbers show what sells | chance: 80
- B | haggle hard with every customer and keep every penny of the margin | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 70
- R | shout the stall's wares down the aisle, louder than the stall opposite | v: stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 72
- G | give the first jar free to the stallholder next door | v: benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 88
- W>R | promise the early customers a new flavour every week, and keep it up | v: stimulation, conformity | foot: person regular | chance: 60
- U>G | find out which of the old recipes the town remembers, and make those | v: tradition | foot: lesson old ways still sell | chance: 70
- B>W | sign for a permanent pitch and pay the whole year's fee up front | v: security, achievement | dream: seal | foot: place comm.market; means money-.06 | chance: 62
- R>U | chat to every trader in the aisle about how each of them started | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person mentor | chance: 82
- G>B | bring the whole family in to help, and keep the profits in the family | v: tradition, security | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 78
works: By four the tin is heavy and the table is nearly bare.
works: A customer comes back an hour later, with a friend, for more.
fails: Rain sets in by ten, and the aisle empties.
fails: By closing time the takings barely cover the pitch fee.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to be somebody in this town (B; cycle s1)

== the evening the room turns to listen
tier: life event
aim: to be somebody in this town
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-80
per_year: 0 0 .3 .4 .4 .3
tone: mixed
life: community
horizon: week
roles: neighbour, elder, parent, a councillor
earth: a crowded residents' meeting in the hall, and a chance to stand up and speak
tribal: a gathering at the clan fire, where the elders let a younger voice be heard
magic: a guildhall meeting where any freeholder may rise and address the bench
scene: The hall is full, the chairs are hard, and the meeting about the bus route has gone round in circles for an hour. {N} has a hand half raised.
scene W: {N} has read the council's papers twice and is sure the rules are on the town's side.
scene U: {N} has the numbers on a folded sheet: how many ride the bus, and when.
scene B: Half the town is here, and the councillor too. A good speech tonight would be remembered.
scene R: {N} is tired of polite murmurs, and the words are already on the tip of the tongue.
scene G: {N} has lived on this street all their life, and so did {parent}, and everyone here knows it.
- W | stand and remind the room what the council promised, word for word | v: conformity, universalism (fairness) | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 70
- U | hand round the figures and let them speak for themselves | v: self-direction | foot: lesson figures carry a room | chance: 65
- B | take the floor, name the problem, and offer to lead the fight yourself | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 55
- R | tell the councillor to their face that the town deserves better | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- G | speak up for the old neighbours who could not make it to the hall | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
- W>U | volunteer to take the minutes and see the vote recorded properly | v: conformity, security | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 78
- U>B | work out who in the room really decides, and sit beside them afterwards | v: power | dream: test | foot: person patron | chance: 68
- B>R | lead a walkout loud enough to get into the local paper | v: power, stimulation | foot: door defied an authority | chance: 45
- R>G | get the whole hall clapping along to the old street song | v: stimulation, tradition | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 50
- G>W | offer your own front room for the next meeting | v: benevolence, conformity | foot: place gather.house | chance: 80
works: The room goes quiet, then nods, and someone at the back says {Ns} name.
works: By the end of the night the councillor asks {N} for a word in private.
fails: The chair moves on to any other business before {N} has finished.
fails: A few people clap, and the rest are already reaching for their coats.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to win at the highest level (B; cycle s2)

== the first time winning is the only thing in the room
tier: life event
aim: to win at the highest level
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult
age: 12-35
per_year: 0 .5 .5 .3 0 0
tone: mixed
life: sport
horizon: moment
roles: rival, friend, grandparent, a coach
earth: the final of the regional championship, one lap left and one rival ahead
tribal: the great race at the summer gathering, with the clans lining the course
magic: the last bout of the realm's games, under the banners of every house
scene: One lap left. The crowd is a blur, and all {N} can see is {rival}'s back, two strides ahead.
scene W: {N} has trained to the plan for months, and the plan says to wait for the last bend.
scene U: {N} has watched {rival} race a dozen times, and {rival} always tires on the hill.
scene B: Second place is the first of the losers. {N} has never wanted anything more.
scene R: {Ns} legs are burning and {N} is laughing, because this is what it is all for.
scene G: The whole family is at the barrier, and {grandparent} is shouting louder than anyone.
- W | hold to the race plan and go on the last bend, as the coach said | v: conformity, achievement | foot: person mentor | chance: 60
- U | go wide on the hill, where the leader always tires | v: achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 58
- B | go now, all of it, and do not look back until the line | v: achievement, power | dream: test | foot: means health-.03 | chance: 50
- R | throw everything into a wild sprint from far out, for the joy of it | v: stimulation | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 40
- G | run your own race and let the place come as it will | v: security | dream: drop | foot: lesson running for its own sake | chance: 80
- W>B | box the leader in on the bend, strictly inside the rules | v: power, conformity | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 52
- U>R | read the wind and the crowd, and save one burst for the line | v: achievement, stimulation | foot: lesson save something for last | chance: 62
- B>G | race for the family's name, louder in your head than any coach | v: achievement, tradition | dream: test | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 60
- R>W | catch the leader and shake hands at the line, whoever wins | v: benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- G>U | listen to your body on the hill, and ease off before it breaks | v: security | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 75
works: {N} crosses the line first, arms up, and cannot hear anything for the noise.
works: The clock shows a time nobody at the club has run before.
fails: {N} finishes second by a stride, and stands alone at the barrier for a long time.
fails: The legs go on the last straight, and three runners pass.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to make money work for me (B; cycle s4)

== the first money that grows on its own
tier: life event
aim: to make money work for me
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-80
per_year: 0 0 .4 .4 .4 .3
tone: joy
life: money
horizon: years
roles: parent, friend, a bank adviser
earth: a small windfall and the first real choice of where to put it
tribal: a first calf of your own, and the choice of whose herd to run it with
magic: a first purse of silver, and the guild bankers' offer to put it to work
scene: There is a cheque on the kitchen table: a small windfall, more money than {N} has ever held in one piece.
scene W: {N} wants it somewhere safe and sensible, where it can be counted on.
scene U: {N} has three tabs open, comparing rates, fees and the small print.
scene B: {N} does not want to spend it. {N} wants it to make more of itself.
scene R: {N} could be on a plane tonight with this. The thought will not go away.
scene G: {parent} always said money should go back into the home and the family.
- W | put it in a fixed savings account and leave it alone | v: security | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 90
- U | read up on it at the library for a month before deciding anything | v: self-direction | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 85
- B | buy a handful of shares and check them every morning | v: power, achievement | dream: test | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 55
- R | spend half on a trip and put the rest away | v: hedonism | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 85
- G | pay down the family's debts first | v: benevolence, security | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 80
- W>G | put a share into the savings circle with the neighbours | v: benevolence, conformity | foot: place comm.credit | chance: 82
- U>W | draw up a plan with a set sum saved every month, and stick to it | v: security, conformity | foot: lesson a little each month adds up | chance: 70
- B>U | find someone who invests for a living, and ask to learn from them | v: achievement | dream: test | foot: person mentor | chance: 60
- R>B | put the lot on a hot tip from a friend, and hope | v: stimulation, power | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 30
- G>R | lend it to a friend starting a business, on a handshake | v: benevolence, stimulation | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 65
works: A year on, the statement shows a little more than went in, and {N} reads it twice.
works: The money grows slowly, and {N} finds that watching it is a pleasure of its own.
fails: The market drops in the first month, and {N} watches a quarter of it vanish.
fails: An emergency comes along, and the money is gone before it can grow.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- to live by my own rules (B R; cycle s1)

== the first door walked out of for good
tier: life event
aim: to live by my own rules
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult
age: 16-40
per_year: 0 .3 .5 .3 0 0
tone: mixed
life: home, work
horizon: years
roles: parent, friend, sibling
earth: a steady job lined up by the family, and a one-way ticket in the other pocket
tribal: the elders' choice of your place in the clan's work, and the open plain beyond the camp
magic: an apprenticeship bought by the family, and the road out of the town gate
scene: The letter offering the job {parent} arranged is in one pocket. A one-way ticket is in the other. The train leaves at six.
scene W: {N} promised {parent} to think it over, and has thought of nothing else.
scene U: {N} has worked out the money to the last coin: three months, if nothing goes wrong.
scene B: Nobody else is going to decide how {Ns} life goes. Not any more.
scene R: The train is at six, the sky is clear, and {Ns} heart is pounding.
scene G: The family's house is warm and full, and leaving it feels like pulling up a root.
- W | tell the family face to face before the train goes | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: door owned up | chance: 70
- U | take the job for a year, and save every penny for leaving | v: security, self-direction | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 75
- B | turn the job down in writing and take the train | v: self-direction, power | dream: test | foot: mark moved away | chance: 70
- R | leave a note on the table and run for the six o'clock | v: stimulation, self-direction | dream: test | foot: door left home | chance: 75
- G | stay, and plant a life of your own inside the family's | v: tradition, security | dream: drop | foot: door stayed home | chance: 80
- W>U | ask the employer in writing to hold the job open for a year | v: security | foot: lesson doors can be held open | chance: 45
- U>B | sell everything that will not fit in one bag | v: self-direction | foot: means freedom+.05 | chance: 85
- B>R | quit, and spend the first week's savings on a night to remember | v: hedonism | foot: means money-.04 | chance: 80
- R>G | ride out with a friend who has been waiting for the same chance | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G>W | go, but swear to be home for every birthday | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 78
works: The train pulls out at six, and {N} watches the town shrink to nothing.
works: On the first morning somewhere new, {N} wakes with no one to answer to and grins at the ceiling.
fails: The money runs out in six weeks, and the ticket home costs more than the one out.
fails: {N} gets as far as the platform, and stands there until the train has gone.

